    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0321" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2668: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras (Lay) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-20T10:00:00-06:00">December 20,
                            1932—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>114. Minister of Foreign Affairs told me yesterday he had telegraphed Paraguayan
                    and Bolivian Governments supporting proposal of Commission of Neutrals and would
                    telegraph to Mr. White accordingly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
